# --- Book content: NEVER commit ------------------------------------------------
#
# This repository is a tool for annotating books you own. It must not become a
# way to distribute one. Two categories matter, and the second is easy to miss:
#
#   1. The books themselves.
#   2. Everything derived from them. `trace.jsonl` carries one record per
#      segment with the source text verbatim — about 772,000 characters, which
#      is the whole novel. `annotations.json` carries the full paragraph around
#      each footnote. Together the untracked artifacts in this directory held
#      ~3.3x the text of the book they came from.
#
# Git history is permanent: a single commit containing these cannot be undone by
# deleting the file later. Keep this section broad and let `git add -f` be the
# deliberate exception, rather than listing files and hoping the list stays
# complete.
*.epub
*.kepub.epub
*.mobi
*.azw3
*.pdf

annotations*.json
trace*.jsonl
*-annotations.json
*-detected.json
review-demo.json
sample-*.json

# Rendered output, and the per-book working directories
out/
out-*/
books/
scratch/

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- OS / editor --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# build artifacts
dist/

# uv writes this when `uv run` is used in the project directory. The documented
# dev flow is venv + pip, so a lock file here would only go stale.
uv.lock
